  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Greening Humanitarian Responses Through Enhanced Solar Energy Harvesting</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In humanitarian settings, energy is a critically enabling factor to address lifesaving needs, ensure provision of basic services and improve social and economic well-being. Energy is generally recognized as a basic human right, however in humanitarian contexts the great majority (over 90 %) of displaced populations have inadequate or no access to modern forms of energy, and almost 1 billion people have no access at all. To continue the efforts towards greening humanitarian responses, this project aims to find a cost-effective way to adapt common single-use solar powered water systems (SPWS) into multipurpose SPWS so that unused and idle energy currently present and wasted at those single-use schemes can be utilized for other uses, in order to meet the most pressing energy needs of crisis-affected populations, humanitarian organizations and/or institutions in crisis zones.</narrative>
  </description>
